{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of your care team doctors. You’re here for your 12th cycle of high-dose methotrexate for your CNS lymphoma. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m okay physically. A bit tired, but no new pain or headaches. I just want to get through this cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure you’re comfortable. I see your mom mentioned something important—about you taking a lot of oxycodone a few days ago. Can we talk about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… yeah. I was really overwhelmed. I took most of my pills, but I threw up that night. I didn’t mean to scare anyone. I just felt so stuck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad you’re honest. That sounds like a very hard moment. You’re not alone in this. We’ve asked Psychiatry to see you because your safety is our top priority."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t feel like hurting myself now. But I’ve been so sad. The chemo, losing my job, the pain… it’s a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes complete sense. You’ve been through so much. Psychiatry will help you find better ways to cope. We also want to support you with social work for the financial stress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I do feel supported at home. My husband and mom are great. I just worry about money and insurance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll connect you with resources. For now, your chemo is scheduled for today. We’ll give you IV fluids to protect your kidneys and help clear the drug."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will I feel sick again like last time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2175-11-03 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nausea is common, but we’ll give you anti-nausea meds like ondansetron. You’ve tolerated it well before, so I’m hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2175-11-03 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chemotherapy infusion is starting now. It’ll take a few hours. Nurses will check on you often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2175-11-03 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. My foot is aching a bit more today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2175-11-03 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve increased your gabapentin to 900mg three times a day to help with that. We’re stopping the oxycodone for now, given what happened."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2175-11-03 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I understand. I don’t want to risk that again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2175-11-04 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs look stable. Liver enzymes are up a bit—this happens with methotrexate—but they should come down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2175-11-04 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2175-11-04 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not usually. It’s mild and temporary. We monitor it closely. You’re clearing the methotrexate well, which is great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2175-11-04 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2175-11-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The Psychiatry team met with you yesterday. They think you’d benefit from a short inpatient stay for more support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2175-11-04 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was afraid they’d say that. But… maybe I do need more help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2175-11-04 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’re increasing your citalopram to 40mg and adding lorazepam for anxiety at night. We’re also watching your heart rhythm since these meds can affect it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2175-11-04 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Is it safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2175-11-04 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with monitoring. Your baseline EKG was normal. We’ll check it again soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2175-11-05 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your methotrexate levels are dropping well—0.15 now, down from 1.9 yesterday. That means your body is clearing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2175-11-05 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I feel more like myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2175-11-05 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also got your MRI results. Your lymphoma is still in stable remission. No progression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2175-11-05 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s the best news I’ve had in a while. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2175-11-05 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll repeat the MRI in a month. For your blood clot history, we’re switching from enoxaparin to aspirin 325mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2175-11-05 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2175-11-05 09:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and easier. But stop it two days before your next chemo admission to avoid interactions with the IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2175-11-05 09:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2175-11-06 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Psychiatry has a bed for you at the inpatient unit. It’s a short stay—just until you’re feeling more stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2175-11-06 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous, but I know I need this. Will my family be able to visit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2175-11-06 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, absolutely. They’re part of your support. You’ll continue your gabapentin, aspirin, and other regular meds there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2175-11-06 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my asthma meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2175-11-06 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, fluticasone-salmeterol, montelukast, and albuterol as needed. All continued."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2175-11-06 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want to have a flare-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2175-11-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. How are you doing emotionally today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2175-11-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still low, but talking to the psychiatrist helped. I’m scared of failing again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2175-11-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This isn’t failure. It’s courage to ask for help. You’re doing the right thing by getting more support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2175-11-07 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That means a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2175-11-08 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your liver enzymes are coming down—ALT and AST are improving. That’s expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2175-11-08 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any other tests before I go to psych?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2175-11-08 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just one more methotrexate level to confirm it’s fully cleared. Then you’re ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your last methotrexate level is 0.05—essentially cleared. Great job."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready for the next step, I think."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve arranged for you to go to the psychiatric facility today. You’ll be there for about a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And then home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and back to oncology in a month for your next cycle and MRI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I restart mesalamine for my colitis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, once you’re home and stable. It was held during chemo due to interaction risks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And acyclovir?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re restarting that for herpes prevention. Take it three times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2175-11-09 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2175-11-10 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check before transfer. You’re alert, walking fine, and your labs are stable. Psych team is expecting you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2175-11-10 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared, but also hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2175-11-10 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely okay. You’re taking a brave step. We’ll follow up with you after your stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2175-11-10 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for not giving up on me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2175-11-10 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We never would. You’re strong, and you’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2175-11-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today you’ll be transferred to the psychiatric facility for continued care. Your discharge summary is ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2175-11-11 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I feel ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2175-11-11 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take your new prescriptions: citalopram 40mg, aspirin, gabapentin 800mg three times a day, and lorazepam for anxiety at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2175-11-11 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And stop aspirin before next chemo?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2175-11-11 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Stop it two days before. Otherwise, keep everything going."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2175-11-11 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2175-11-11 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2175-11-03 10:37:00",
    "admission_end": "2175-11-11 19:28:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma, ulcerative colitis, asthma, and a history of DVT/PE was admitted for her 12th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She tolerated the treatment well, with expected mild transaminitis and manageable nausea. An MRI showed stable remission of her lymphoma. She disclosed a recent suicide attempt by oxycodone overdose, prompting a psychiatry consultation. Due to ongoing depressive symptoms and inadequate outpatient mental health resources, she was deemed unsafe for discharge home and arranged for transfer to an inpatient psychiatric facility. Her anticoagulation was changed from enoxaparin to aspirin per neuro-oncology recommendation. Gabapentin was increased for chronic right foot pain, and citalopram was uptitrated to 40mg daily. She cleared methotrexate adequately and was transferred to extended psychiatric care in stable condition.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Pain in limb",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Poisoning by other opiates and related narcotics",
      "Suicide and self-inflicted poisoning by analgesics, antipyretics, and antirheumatics",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Antineoplastic and immunosuppressive drugs causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Other nonspecific abnormal serum enzyme levels"
    ]
  }
}
